{
    "background_story": "Cherry was a devoted supporter of President Woodrow Wilson's progressive policies during the early 20th century. A Wilsonian through and through, she believed in the importance of international cooperation, social reform, and individual liberty. Cherry worked tirelessly as a volunteer for the League of Nations, advocating for its establishment and promoting its ideals of collective security and diplomacy. Her passion for Wilson's vision of a more just and peaceful world inspired others to join the cause. Cherry's dedication to the Wilsonian ideals also led her to participate in the women's suffrage movement, fighting for the rights of women to participate in the democratic process. Her commitment to these principles earned her recognition as a leading figure in the progressive movement of her time.",
